<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>CasualtiesUnknownOnline.RecursiveCrafting.Core</AssemblyName>
    <Product>Recursive Crafting Core</Product>
    <Version>0.1.0</Version>
    <LangVersion>preview</LangVersion>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>CasualtiesUnknownOnline.RecursiveCrafting.Core</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The satellite mod's game-free half: the recursive-chain resolver a recipe panel asks "can this be reached
    through other steps, and through which ones". Deliberately no reference at all (not even BepInEx): the
    resolver is plain C# over the mod's own little model, so its rules can be tested and reasoned about without
    the game, the network or CUO's runtime. The plug-in half (a later stage of the ticket) adapts the game's
    recipe table and inventory into this model.
  -->
</Project>
